WEBVTT

00:00:00.431 --> 00:00:03.810
Journey thirty-one: get ready for launch.

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:09.661
Before Jubilee opens, a visitor leaves an e-mail address for the launch

00:00:09.661 --> 00:00:15.018
notice, or sends a business's details to be listed on launch day.

00:00:15.018 --> 00:00:20.375
This run gave every criterion of L2-215 to L2-218 a passing test.

00:00:21.231 --> 00:00:24.854
The marketing site says it plainly: launching soon.

00:00:24.854 --> 00:00:29.615
Tell me when it launches moves the page to the launch notification,

00:00:29.615 --> 00:00:33.807
clear of the top bar. Nothing on the page links to the app.

00:00:34.509 --> 00:00:40.070
Sent empty, the form sends nothing. A summary lists what to fix, each a

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:43.125
link to its field, and takes the focus.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:47.027
Joanna types her address and ticks the box.

00:00:47.027 --> 00:00:52.091
While it is sent, the button is busy, the fields cannot be changed, and

00:00:52.091 --> 00:00:54.160
a second press sends nothing.

00:00:54.959 --> 00:00:58.591
If Jubilee cannot be reached, she sees no error.

00:00:58.591 --> 00:01:04.039
The form says it is still sending, and tries again every five seconds; a

00:01:04.039 --> 00:01:07.899
new test proves it when no answer comes within ten.

00:01:07.899 --> 00:01:09.791
Then: you're on the list.

00:01:13.105 --> 00:01:17.949
Past five sign-ups in an hour from one address, the form says when to

00:01:17.949 --> 00:01:20.617
try again, and keeps everything typed.

00:01:23.514 --> 00:01:28.297
The business pre-registration asks for the business, its owner and

00:01:28.297 --> 00:01:33.516
consent. When the server refuses a field the page let through, the field

00:01:33.516 --> 00:01:37.068
says so, with the summary, and every value stays.

00:01:37.068 --> 00:01:37.938
That is new.

00:01:40.744 --> 00:01:45.613
When the bot challenge is not passed, the form says so and keeps every

00:01:45.613 --> 00:01:50.482
value. New specs prove that each form sends the challenge's token, and

00:01:50.482 --> 00:01:53.056
asks for a fresh one after a refusal.

00:01:55.869 --> 00:02:00.209
Sent, the confirmation takes the focus: the Jubilee team will be in

00:02:00.209 --> 00:02:03.837
touch before launch, and the business is not listed yet.

00:02:04.696 --> 00:02:09.459
Behind the marketing host, the limits now have tests on both sides of

00:02:09.459 --> 00:02:14.015
the proxy. Each visitor's address has its own five an hour, and an

00:02:14.015 --> 00:02:17.536
address a caller states for itself is not believed.

00:02:18.396 --> 00:02:22.779
The Jubilee team reads the lists with the command line only.

00:02:22.779 --> 00:02:26.725
Its output is the export, and each reading is audited.

00:02:26.725 --> 00:02:31.986
A worker test proves the daily job deletes what is twelve months old and

00:02:31.986 --> 00:02:33.228
logs counts only.

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:39.486
The owner now has one ordered checklist in the Azure readme, eight

00:02:39.486 --> 00:02:44.067
steps, each with its command and how to check it worked.

00:02:44.067 --> 00:02:45.703
ADR 0061 records it.

00:02:46.562 --> 00:02:51.731
What is left is the owner's: run the checklist in production, send each

00:02:51.731 --> 00:02:56.755
form once, and read it back. Journey thirty-one stands at one hundred

00:02:56.755 --> 00:02:57.338
percent.
